1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Every screenshot AI tool asks you to upload your whole screen.
But screenshots are full of API keys, customer emails, IBANs and tokens.
This one does the opposite.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,000
A developer debugging a 401, a support agent with a customer ticket,
a bank statement. Three very common screenshots, all full of secrets.

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Gemini Nano reads the image locally. It finds emails, API keys, tokens,
IBANs, card numbers, addresses and names, replaces them with placeholders
and paints black boxes over the pixels.
The labels show only the type, never the value.

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The model can miss something. I can drag a manual box, or click one to remove it,
and the redacted image, the receipt and the risk card update immediately.

5
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:45,000
A short question stays on-device in about two seconds, with no raw image sent.
A complex question goes to the cloud with only the sanitized payload,
streamed back in a few seconds. That is real hybrid inference,
with a privacy guard.

6
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The cloud only gets what I explicitly choose: text, redacted image, or both.
The risk card shows zero secrets sent and the receipt hashes the sanitized text
and the redacted image. App Check signs every cloud call, so the claim is auditable.

7
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Detectors, Luhn, box normalization, leak check, routing policy and receipt
hashing are covered by Node tests. The on-device model uses structured JSON
output through Firebase AI Logic; the cloud leg is a separate, explicit step.

8
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Redact locally, ask globally. The code is open source under GPL-3.0.
Thanks for watching.
